    <string name="permission_accessibility_why">ZeroOS needs accessibility to keep your limits outside ZeroOS, to block short videos and for double-tap to lock.</string>
    <string name="permission_accessibility_reads">It sees which app is in front. Only while the short-video blocker is on, it also looks at the layout of YouTube and Instagram (button and list names, never what\'s in a video or comment). Android allows this for all apps at once; ZeroOS only looks inside those two.</string>
